Contributing to the project{\*\bkmkend contributing_to_the_project}
\par }\pard\plain \s17\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
Apache is a volunteer-driven project. That means that it relies largely on the users to contribute patches, suggestions, bug reports, and comments.
\par And big piles of money, of course.
\par If you think that you have any of the above, and you want to contribute them, here's how to go about it.
\par Within each project in the Apache Software Foundation, development is completely autonomous from the Foundation as a whole. Each project is left to man
age affairs as best suits that project. Each project has its own web site off of the main www.apache.org web site, and you can usually find information on those sites about contributing code or documentation patches.
\par For example, for the XML projects, there is information listed at }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "http://xml.apache.org/overview.html" }}{\fldrslt {\cs15\ul\cf2 http://xml.apache.org/overview.html}}}{
 on how you can get involved in the project. There are links to the mailing lists (http://xml.apache.org/mail.html), the CVS repository (http://xml.apache.org/cvs.html), and the binary builds of the code (http://xml.apache.org/dist/).
\par If you would like to contribute financially to the foundation, you can find out more information about doing that at }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "http://www.apache.org/foundation/contributing.html" }}{\fldrslt {\cs15\ul\cf2 
http://www.apache.org/foundation/contributing.html}}}{ The ASF is not, at this time, a non-profit organization, so contributions are not tax-deductable. However, they might be elligible to be considered as part of the cost of doing busines
s, if you use Apache software in your organization.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {{\pict{\*\picprop\shplid1035{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}
