\par }\pard\plain \s1\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs48\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning36\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {{\*\bkmkstart more_information}More information
{\*\bkmkend more_information}
\par }\pard\plain \s17\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
Since Apache is entirely an online phenomenon, there is a lot of information online about it. Of course, the definitive source of information is the Apache Software Foundation, at }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "http://www.apache.org/" }
}{\fldrslt {\cs15\ul\cf2 http://www.apache.org/}}}{ but there other sites with additional information.
\par Covalent Technologies: }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "http://www.covalent.com/" }}{\fldrslt {\cs15\ul\cf2 http://www.covalent.com/}}}{ Covalent is the first company to offer commercial support fo
r Apache. They also are the producers of Raven, one of the leading SSL solutions. And they host the development of Comanche, the GUI configuration tool for Apache.
\par ApacheWeek: }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "http://www.apacheweek.com/" }}{\fldrslt {\cs15\ul\cf2 http://www.apacheweek.com/}}}{ If you rea
lly want to keep up with what's happening with Apache, you need to subscribe to ApacheWeek. You'll get a weekly mailing with all the latest news. You'll know about the new releases before they happen. You'll know what the is going to be put into new versi
ons, and what bugs have been found and fixed in the old versions. An absolute must for anyone dealing with Apache on a regular basis.
\par ApacheCon: }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "http://www.apachecon.com/" }}{\fldrslt {\cs15\ul\cf2 http://www.apachecon.com/}}}{ Well, ApacheCon 2000 is already past, but th
ere are more planned for the future. Submit papers and sign up to come to the next one!
